&lt;p&gt;Ensure Field Medical activities adhere to global and regional regulations (FDA, EMA, GxP, ICH, PhRMA, Sunshine Act), company policies, and medical governance.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support audit and inspection readiness activities for Field Medical operations.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills, Experience and Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advanced degree required (PharmD, PhD, MD, or equivalent in life sciences).&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;10+ years of progressive experience in biotech/pharma Medical Affairs, with at least 5+ years in Field Medical or MSL Excellence leadership.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Demonstrated success developing global Field Medical strategies, competency frameworks, and learning programs.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
