&lt;p&gt;Our people are united by a shared way of working: follow the science, challenge assumptions, act with urgency and hold ourselves to a high standard of rigor—all in service of patients.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;The Opportunity:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Revolution Medicines is seeking a strategic, collaborative, and execution-oriented Senior Director, Global Pricing Strategy &amp;amp; Execution to build and lead global pricing capabilities and support the execution of strategies to support our emerging oncology portfolio. This leader will establish the frameworks for &amp;nbsp;pricing and contracting strategy for current and future investigational therapies targeting RAS-addicted cancers..&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This role will partner closely with Global Market Access, Commercial, Medical Affairs, Finance, Regulatory, Legal, Supply Chain, and Regional/Country teams to translate strategy into compliant, launch-ready execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Key Responsibilities&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Establish global pricing architecture, including list-price strategy, country sequencing, price corridors, launch price recommendations, lifecycle pricing, and governance processes.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with Global Market Access to develop integrated pricing and reimbursement strategies that support value communication, payer engagement, and sustainable patient access.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Lead development of global price business cases and financial models, including gross-to-net, demand, revenue, access, and affordability scenarios.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Define pricing guardrails, discounting principles, Innovative Access Agreements (IAAs), approval authorities, and exception-management processes that enable disciplined local execution.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Partner with regional and country teams to adapt global pricing strategies to local healthcare systems, reference-pricing dynamics, HTA requirements, tender environments, and regulatory constraints.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Collaborate with Commercial Operations and IT to design and implement fit-for-purpose pricing, contracting, and analytics tools.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Establish dashboards and operating rhythms to monitor price realization, gross-to-net performance, access outcomes, contracting performance, and pricing risks.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Support launch readiness planning by ensuring pricing strategy, governance, systems, and cross-functional accountabilities are in place ahead of anticipated approvals.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Provide thought leadership and clear recommendations to senior executives; communicate complex pricing tradeoffs in a concise, decision-oriented manner.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Build and develop a high-performing pricing team and foster pricing capabilities across the global organization&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Required Skills, Experience and Education:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Advanced degree (PhD, PharmD, MD, MBA, or equivalent) in Health Economics, Public Policy, Life Sciences, or related field.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;12+ years of experience in global pricing, market access, health economics, or government policy within the biopharmaceutical industry.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Deep understanding of global pricing and reimbursement systems (e.g., US, EU4+UK, Japan, emerging markets).&lt;/p&gt;
